            <ArticleTitle>[Supporting the establishment of the parent-child bond in cases of prematurity].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>15-19</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1259-4792(17)30141-4</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.spp.2017.09.003</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The evolution of the care of premature babies is having an effect on a particular difficulty, that of the development of parenthood and the parent-baby relationship hampered by an early birth. The short- and long-term consequences of any disruption to these two dimensions can be considerable and the hospital must take into account the issue when caring for parents and their premature baby.</AbstractText>
